# Mongolia Selected to Host the 34th GBIF Governing Board Meeting in 2027

Mongolia has been selected to host the **34th Global Biodiversity Information Facility (GBIF) Governing Board Meeting (GB34)** in 2027.

The selection represents an important milestone for **GBIF Mongolia** and the **Institute of Biology of the Mongolian Academy of Sciences**, and reflects Mongolia’s growing engagement with the international biodiversity information community.

## Mongolia to Welcome the Global GBIF Community

The GBIF Governing Board brings together representatives of GBIF Participants from around the world to guide the strategic development of the global biodiversity information network.

By hosting GB34, Mongolia will have the opportunity to welcome members of the international GBIF community and strengthen connections between Mongolian researchers, institutions, and biodiversity data experts from across the world.

Mongolia’s selection also provides an opportunity to showcase the country’s rich biodiversity and scientific community, while highlighting the importance of accessible and openly available biodiversity information.

## Strengthening Mongolia’s Role in Biodiversity Data

GBIF Mongolia, hosted by the **Institute of Biology of the Mongolian Academy of Sciences**, works to support the mobilization, publication, and use of biodiversity data from Mongolia through the global GBIF network.

Mongolia’s biodiversity includes diverse ecosystems extending from mountain and forest-steppe regions to the vast grasslands and Gobi Desert. Making information about this biodiversity more accessible can support scientific research, conservation, environmental management, and evidence-based decision-making.

Hosting GB34 will further strengthen Mongolia’s participation in this international network and create opportunities for knowledge exchange and future collaboration.

## Looking Ahead to 2027

The hosting of GB34 is an important opportunity for Mongolia to connect with the global biodiversity information community and contribute to discussions shaping the future of biodiversity data.

**GBIF Mongolia and the Institute of Biology of the Mongolian Academy of Sciences look forward to welcoming the GBIF community to Mongolia in 2027.**

Further information about GB34 and related activities will be shared as preparations progress.

